The first game was an immersive experience filled with tough decisions. The Walking Dead: Season One was a milestone in singleplayer gaming. Playing through the game does not even have to be a singleplayer experience as I have heard of many who play the game together; It is like an interactive TV-series! Although, the first game was
, the sequel is nothing less. Telltale Games have topped the icing with their choice-carrying from episode to episode. Guess what!? With the release of "The Walking Dead: Season Two," it even works from season to season! The choices we made in the first game carries on to the next game! I highly recommend to
first if you have yet to play it, but otherwise: go ahead and buy it! "The Walking Dead: Season Two" is easily a 5/5 stars game. It is simple, yet complex with the advanced feature of choice-carrying. You can play the game on most devices available. Also, the story is enchanthing! It puts you through the tale of Clementine as she continues to fight for her life;

This game can't be criticized on basis of Graphics and Gameplay. This is literally something special, this game makes you think in real life about decisions after playing, didn't expected this much emotions from a game. I don't know why but i saved Chloe ;_;
Want to play this game again but without any memories, someone call Men in Black to erase them. xD
If thinking to buy this game go for it, 2.5$ can't give any better experince.

Simply the best multiplayer 4x game;
But also in single player it has high re-playability because of the different civilizations to play and different victory conditions to achieve.
ps. for those who fear the mp issues of V: it looks like they've got most sync problems in check this time, and restore quite gracefully from them if they do occur (only once seen a player desync more than once during a game, most games finished without any desyncing at-all).

Try not to cry.
Cry a lot.
;_;
